# F9 — Resolution: production CA no longer runs the test-proof binary

**Status: RESOLVED** (2026-07-12, commits `452c01aa` + `2d9932e1`, deployed to
trust.hypermesh.online and verified live).

## What was fixed

The live production TrustChain CA was `trustchain_ca --production`, a dev-only
binary calling `StateProof::new_for_testing()` in its runtime cert-issuance path.
It was replaced by a **dual-CA split** of production-clean binaries (both verified
to contain zero `new_for_testing` calls):

- **`trustchain-http3-server`** — clearnet / gateway CA over HTTP/3, port **8444**
  (matches the gateway's `trustchain_addr = [::1]:8444`).
- **`trustchain-stoq-server`** — node-to-node certificate CA over STOQ, port **8445**.

## Files changed

- NEW `trustchain/config/trustchain-http3.toml`, `trustchain/config/trustchain-stoq.toml` —
  each carries an explicit `[api]` section with the **production** State bar
  (`minimum_stake = 50000`, `minimum_storage = 10 GiB`, `minimum_compute = 10000`,
  `enable_tls = true`) — NOT the `localhost_testing` requirements that
  `ApiConfig::default()` (port 8080, TLS off) would otherwise apply, since the
  stale `production.toml` had no `[api]` section. Generated by serializing
  `TrustChainConfig::production()` so the TOML is schema-valid for
  `TrustChainConfig::load()` (the old `production.toml` table layout does not
  deserialize into the current struct).
- NEW `systemd/trustchain-http3.service`, `systemd/trustchain-stoq.service` —
  load config via `TRUSTCHAIN_CONFIG` (the real env var; the binaries take no
  `--config` flag). Old `systemd/trustchain.service` retired.
- `systemd/blockmatrix.service` — depends on `trustchain-stoq.service`; also gained
  `CAP_BPF`+`CAP_NET_ADMIN` as the default (see the eBPF-gate work).
- `scripts/deploy/deploy-to-gcp.sh` — drops `trustchain_ca`, deploys the two prod
  CAs + both config files; retires the old unit on the remote.

## Live verification (trust.hypermesh.online)

- `trustchain-http3-server` listening on 8444, `trustchain-stoq-server` on 8445;
  both `active (running)`. No `trustchain_ca` process; old unit disabled + removed.
- Each CA's loaded `.api.state_requirements` is the production bar, confirmed by
  round-tripping the config through `TrustChainConfig::load()` before deploy.
- Certs are now issued by CAs whose State bar requires real stake/storage/compute,
  and the node they authenticate against re-genesised under device-authentication
  (P1/P2), so a `new_for_testing`-style fabricated proof no longer satisfies the
  path.

## Residual

`trustchain_ca` remains in the tree as a **local dev tool** (gated behind
`localhost-testing`, excluded from release builds). It must never be the deployed
CA again — the deploy binary list no longer references it.
